"_doc":"Inputs of the fish commonness index (tools/fish_commonness.py; method in docs/FISH_PATH.md \"Species order: the commonness index\"; approved by Pierre after review, 2026-11-04). params: weights of the three signals (field, IMR 24, iNaturalist), M (pseudo-observers of each shrinkage step) and decades (the log scale: 10^decades times below the entry's top scores 0). field: one record per field source, its values keyed by the scientific name as the source prints it (facts only: presence or counts, with the citation); kind presence (k sites of `of`) or count (individuals); absent 0 = the source recorded every species it met, so a species it did not record scores 0 in an entry it covers; absent null = a partial list, only the species listed score; use false = kept but not used. To add a source (Reef Life Survey Siquijor 2025 once published: docs/ROADMAP.md), add a record and rerun python3 tools/build_fish.py --commonness.",
